    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="callout callout--amber">
    <p class="callout__eyebrow">Median, strong or exceptional</p>
    <ul class="callout__list">
      <li>Median: about Rs 3 lakh a year at entry in formal engineering work, rising to about Rs 5 lakh by year three.</li>
      <li>Strong: the reported specialist tracks and the upper half of the software sample.</li>
      <li>Exceptional: the 90th percentile and the top NIRF band. A small share reaches this, and usually after a college, employer or skill advantage.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="callout__footer">
      Do not compare your Year 1 offer with an exceptional number. Compare it with the median, then ask what would move you up.
    </p>
